{
  "vocab": "form",
  "version": "v1",
  "status": "PROVISIONAL — covers the three demo ingredients only. Adding an ingredient means adding a block here, not changing code.",
  "policy": {
    "salt_family": "Drives the 0.50 partial-transfer tier. For botanicals it means PREPARATION family, not a chemical salt.",
    "unspecified": "Every ingredient has exactly one *_unspecified form. It takes the 0.30 penalty. S7 must use it rather than guess a salt.",
    "conversion": "The MODEL never does the elemental arithmetic. S7 reports the compound dose and the form id; pipeline/vocab.py converts using molar masses recorded here. Arithmetic stays deterministic (invariant 1) and auditable.",
    "conversion_safe": "false means a hydrate of this salt is common in supplements AND the hydration state is routinely unstated. The ambiguity reaches 2.1x for chloride and 2.0x for sulfate. When false there is no single defensible elemental number, so elemental_dose_mg returns null (invariant 5).",
    "hydrate_molar_mass_g_mol": "Where the common hydrate is known, the ambiguity is BOUNDED rather than unknown: the true elemental dose lies between the hydrate and anhydrous conversions. elemental_dose_range_mg() returns that interval, which is usually narrow enough to land in one dose band anyway. Discarding a study we can bound would be over-caution, not caution.",
    "standardisation": "Botanical withanolide percentages are LABEL CLAIMS that vary by batch. They are recorded for matching and are never used in arithmetic."
  },
